      "provenance": {
        "notes": "Severities and symptoms are the agent's mapping: the ASPCA page names the agents (ficin, psoralen) and lists dogs, cats and horses as toxic but gives no clinical signs; NC State only tags cats, dogs and horses; RHS (cultivar 'Exotica') says harmful if eaten and a skin allergen for humans and dogs. Skin grade 2 follows the 01e baseline for latex; it is not stated by a fetched page. Watering: NC State 'enough to keep it from drying out fully', RHS moderate and moist but well-drained; mapped to let_top_dry. Size and habit are the RHS cultivar figures (1.5 to 2.5 m by 1 to 1.5 m); NC State says 2 to 10 ft as a houseplant. Temperature: cold-intolerant on both, no range. Humidity: no page gives one."
      },
